        "text": "Great, I've got the update on the token usage and context status. Let's proceed with finding the appropriate grid size and block size to ensure full coverage of the elements. \n\nGiven:\n- \\( n = 1048576 \\)\n- We need the maximum index \\(\\text{max_idx}\\) to be \\( n - 1 = 1048575 \\).\n\nThe formula for the maximum index is:\n\\[\n\\text{max_idx} = (\\text{grid_size} \u00d7 \\text{block_size}) + (\\text{block_size} - \uff11)\n\\]\n\nWe need to find \\(\\text{grid_size}\\) and \\text{block_size} such that:\n\\[\n(\\text{grid_size} \u00d7 \\text{block_size}) + (\\text {block_size} - 1) = 1048575\n\\]\n\nLet's start by trying some values. For example, let's try \\(\\text{block_size} = 256\\):\n\nIf \\(\\text{block_size} = 256\\):\n\\[\n\\text{max_idx} = (\\text{grid_size}\u00d7256) + 255\n\\]\nWe need:\n\\[\n(\\text{grid_size} \u00d7 256) + 255 = 1048575\n\\]\nSolving for \\(\\text{grid_size}\\):\n\\[\n\\text{grid_size} \u00d7 256 = 1048320\n\\]\n\\[\n\\text{grid_size} = \\frac{1048320}{256} = 4096\n\\]\n\nSo, one possible pair is \\(\\text{grid_size} = 4096\\) and \\(\\text{block_size} = 256\\).\n\nLet's verify this solution:\n\\[\n\\text{max_idx} = (4096 \u00d7 256) + 255 = 1056256 + 255 = 1048575\n \\]\n\nThis verifies that our solution works. Now, let's design the Triton kernel using these parameters. \n\n### Triton Kernel Design\n\nHere is a basic outline of what the kernel might look like:\n\n```cpp\n#include <triton/triton.h>\n\nusing namespace triton;\n\n__global__"
